text:
rachel: Quick mobile pass notes from the console QA this morning — three small but visible issues on narrow widths (phones): 1) action bar collapse animation briefly overlays the table controls causing a tap miss, 2) inline search steals header space and pushes the project chip off-screen on very small devices, 3) long model/token strings still cause a tiny horizontal scroll when stacked rows + keyboard are present. Screenshot + short gif: https://img.redwood.test/console/2026-09/actionbar-overlap.gif

kai: Repro'd on iPhone 11 and Pixel 4a. The action bar does a translateY animation while the table header is position:sticky; the animation creates a stacking context so the header's computed offset changes mid-animation. Also saw the search input expanding eats ~56px of space which feels aggressive.

mike: Quick proposals: a) at <=460px collapse the search into a compact search-chip (magnifier icon + label) that expands to a full-screen overlay when tapped, b) for action bar animation add `will-change: transform` and move backdrop insertion earlier so header doesn't recompute, or simpler set header to `position: relative` while the action drawer is animating. Example CSS I tried:```css
/* compact search chip */
@media (max-width: 460px) {
  .header-search { display: none; }
  .search-chip { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; padding: 6px 10px; border-radius: 8px; }
}
/* avoid sticky reflow during sidebar open */
.sidebar-opening .main-header { position: relative; }
```

anya: Accessibility and hit-target notes: - Compact search chip must have `aria-expanded` and on expand focus should be moved to the first interactive element inside the overlay. - Ensure chip has `aria-label="Open search"`. - Hit target: current compact rows are ~32px tall; change to `min-height: 44px` for stacked rows and make the whole row a single `role=button` with descriptive `aria-label`. - For long tokens: use `word-break: break-word` and render as a truncated pill with a copy button. The copy button needs `aria-label="Copy model ID: <full-value>"` so screen readers know what will be copied.

mike: Gesture deadzone: we're still getting accidental left-edge nav when users try to swipe a row. My suggestion: only treat edge-swipe as nav when `touchstart.clientX < 18`. Also add a small 6px left visual affordance gradient so users discover edge swipe without losing row swipe.

rachel: Nice. Also UX copy tweak: column toggle label is confusing on mobile. Proposal: rename "Show columns" -> "Columns & display" and under the compact bottom-sheet include a one-line helper: "Choose visible columns and row density (saved per device)". We'll include a density slider in the sheet (compact/comfortable).

kai: Implementation sketch for keyboard-safe layout (uses visualViewport):```js
function syncHeaderToViewport(){
  const top = window.visualViewport ? window.visualViewport.offsetTop : 0;
  document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--viewport-offset', top + 'px');
}
window.visualViewport && window.visualViewport.addEventListener('resize', syncHeaderToViewport);
```

anya: Small a11y nit: when the compact search becomes a full-screen overlay, ensure `aria-modal=true` and add `inert`/`aria-hidden` to the background. Screen readers should hear "Search dialog" then the input. Also update toast copy from generic "Copied" to "Copied model ID" for context.

design-ops-bot: Reminder: if we adjust breakpoints or add `--viewport-offset` token, update sources/design/tokens.md. Also file screenshot artifacts to sources/slack/product for the experiment.

rachel: Action items: Mike - prototype compact search chip + set header relative during sidebar animations (assign 2d); Kai - add touchstart gate for edge-swipe and left-edge affordance (1d); Anya - accessibility checklist + copy updates for toasts and copy button (1d); Rachel - draft A/B plan for 10-day run: Variant A = compact-search + stacked cards (full-row tap targets); Variant B = compact-search + compact rows with increased padding. Metrics: accidental tap rate, time-to-open-detail, search activation rate. I'll post PR + video by EOD. Thanks! :thumbsup:
